  "body": "Right now we call `spam_checker.check_registration_for_spam` with both native, local, Synapse registrations _and_ with the \"first login\" of SSO users.\r\n\r\nIf a homeserver is running with both native and SSO-provided logins, it'd be good to expose to the spam checker the nature of the registration - perhaps by passing in `auth_provider_id` to the `check_registration_for_spam` call?",
